<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Discipline Priest Healer in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Discipline Priest Healer Phase 2</h2>
<i>Healer gearing always heavily depends on playstyle, situation and raid environment so treat the BiS list below as a guideline rather than a gospel.</i>
<br/>
<br/>While there is a variety of strong items  that can be considered Phase 2 BiS, some of them naturally end up being rare hardmode drops or highly sought after pieces such that will generally go to caster dps first. Due to that, the gear embed below has both a contested and a more realistic setup to choose from, though most players will likely end up with something inbetween. <br/>
<br/>Another thing worth mentioning is that you effectively cannot avoid going above the hastecap in phase bis setups anymore, since many of our favoured options simply provide haste rating alongside the other stats that already make them the best choice. Nonetheless, there is still some value in the extra haste, which comes from both quicker <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53007/penance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_penance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Penance</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48123/smite">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_holysmite.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smite</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48072/prayer-of-healing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_prayerofhealing02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Prayer of Healing</span></a> hardcasts as well as the benefit on any spells cast without <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=52800/borrowed-time">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_borrowedtime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Borrowed Time</span></a>.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="the-importance-of-4pc-t8">The Importance of 4p T8</h3>Although the 2p perk is not very remarkable, the four set bonus grants us a massive 250 spell power for 5 seconds after any <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48066/power-word-shield">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_powerwordshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Power Word: Shield</span></a> cast. <br/>Similar to Borrowed Time, this will practically always be active and converts to about 375 additional absorption for your shields, which is why we will most likely not replace it until T10. <br/>
<br/>Despite that, tier 8 is just as great for everyone else on your token so you should not just rely on getting handed the tokens in your 25m raid but instead aim to get any four pieces as soon as possible by running your weekly <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4603/vault-of-archavon">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Vault of Archavon</span></a>, 10m <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> and buying them with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=221/emblem-of-conquest">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></span></a>.<br/>
<br/>As a quick recap, these are all the possible sources of your T8 pieces:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Helmet  and Chest - Can be obtained in both 10m and 25m Ulduar and purchased using Emblems of Conquest.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Shoulder - Can only drop in both of your weekly Ulduar lockouts, making it the rarest piece.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Legs and Gloves - These two pieces will likely drop in Vault of Archavon and Ulduar 10m/<wbr/>25m.</div></li></ul>
